 "relevance_note": "This single-centre cohort of 79 pediatric monogenic autoinflammatory disease patients includes two HA20 patients, each with one stated TNFAIP3 variant: \"The genetic sequencing yielded p.R271X of the TNFAIP3 gene in one patient and p.R45X in the other one\".",
 "method_note": "Read the whole paper by hand; a short Python script only assembled the JSON and checked spans. No table was transcribed by script. The two HA20 patients are never labelled. Their labels ('one patient', 'the other one') are taken from the only sentence that ties a fact to one specific person, the variant sentence ('p.R271X of the TNFAIP3 gene in one patient and p.R45X in the other one'). The same words in other sentences may refer to either person. Table 2 has disease groups as rows (row 'A20 deficiency (n = 2)'); its columns are 'Age onset (median, range)', 'Gender (male: female)', 'Main clinical findings', 'Genetic defects', 'Inheritance'. Sex = female for both, from Gender 0:2 with n = 2. Not attributed to either person, because the paper does not say which patient had them: age at onset (group median 4, range 0-8); Table 2's group-level findings 'Fever, rash, arthralgia, mucosal ulcers, bowel inflammation, CTD'; 'One patient was diagnosed as Behçet disease previously and the other one was diagnosed with undifferentiated connective tissue disease'; and 'Hashimoto′s thyroiditis was also found in one patient'. These checklist items stay 'not reported' for both (a count without names does not exclude). Recurrent oral ulcer comes from 'both suffered', and elevated inflammation indices and no malignancy come from the inclusion criteria for all 288 enrolled patients ('They all had...'). These rows are marked 'inferred from group statement'. 'No evidence of ... infection' at inclusion was NOT recorded as an exclusion, because the Discussion says 'one third of the sick kids would experience episodes of infections' (unnamed); recurrent infections stays 'not reported'. Consanguinity 'no' and 'Chinese' are cohort-wide statements. Treatment (anti-TNF-α) is stated for 'HA20 patients' as a group, not per patient. Table 2's 'AD' is the disease's inheritance mode, not variant origin, so inheritance and zygosity are 'not reported'. variant_type is 'not reported' because the authors use 'X' notation but never name the class. cites_prior_report_of_same_patients is null: nothing is said about earlier reports of the HA20 patients. Refs 25 and 26 are cited for variant pathogenicity only. (The NLRP12 patients' variants 'have been analyzed and reported previously (12)'; those are not TNFAIP3 patients.) Contradictions found (none concern the HA20 patients): the Discussion says 'All of these AID patients are under regular follow-up', but Table 3 case 8 reads 'Death prior to treatment'. Vital status is therefore left 'not reported'.",
